\newlabel{fig:schematic_combined}{{2}{5}{\textbf {Terminal reward domination.} The reward signal in $\mathcal {L}_{\mathrm {term}}$ tends to dominate the KL regularizer, causing the optimizer to over-tilt toward the high-reward mode relative to the balanced RLHF target $q^*$. \textbf {(a)} plots the theoretical prediction from \S \ref {subsec:trd}; \textbf {(b)} shows the 1-D empirical result (Appendix~\ref {app:toy_experiment}), confirming the collapse in practice even at $\tau =1$.\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
